[{:db/id "q-332870/field-1/daa0be0b873ab0198ef002ddf132f796081febdad90bb161cb27527412dd138e" :answer/id #uuid "4f6e1235-d123-53b2-b171-737560dbf5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}\\cos(x)+\\frac{19}{10}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332870/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f523fe47-387d-59da-8547-a0ec9b08a934" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332870/field-1/daa0be0b873ab0198ef002ddf132f796081febdad90bb161cb27527412dd138e" :answer-field/choices ["q-332870/field-1/daa0be0b873ab0198ef002ddf132f796081febdad90bb161cb27527412dd138e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332870" :question/id #uuid "cd21ba85-8f41-5ff6-aef4-4eb449f71fff" :question/math-academy-id "q-332870" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(\\beta -3\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(\\alpha +3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta -3\\alpha =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ \\alpha +3\\beta =5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives: $\\alpha =-\\frac{7}{10},$ $\\beta =\\frac{19}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{7}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\frac{19}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332870/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332870"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332676/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823" :answer/id #uuid "1361dbbd-6eaf-5807-a676-69facfd923b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186319049 :answer-field/choices ["q-332676/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332623/field-1/e34d820da33315d542c768a646a3e7d7ed97724a04ca3b0a8c0cbfd21f7d448a" :answer/id #uuid "7d28e55d-3afa-5dae-a859-56ddd75ff45b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}\\cos(x)+\\frac{7}{5}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332623/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823" :answer/id #uuid "7212005c-1986-515b-851e-c89d6a1fcb6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228054 :answer-field/correct "q-332623/field-1/e34d820da33315d542c768a646a3e7d7ed97724a04ca3b0a8c0cbfd21f7d448a" :answer-field/choices ["q-332623/field-1/e34d820da33315d542c768a646a3e7d7ed97724a04ca3b0a8c0cbfd21f7d448a" "q-332623/field-1/3b1e7f2cc6ae7e186407c31071eb119fa9c19a78ac0964aad6b41c3ad58ab823"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-332623"] :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha +2\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha +\\beta =7\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha +2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{14}{5},\\beta =\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{14}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332622/field-1/bb71dd18b06237165fae60aec9d1c4d85a5cb816694158cb48520a2689647f20" :answer/id #uuid "cbc17935-2db8-511e-a96b-f886bfba5a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{17}\\cos(x)+\\frac{32}{17}\\sin(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332622/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7db62d-20b3-5a50-9d66-6354ba7e63ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332622/field-1/bb71dd18b06237165fae60aec9d1c4d85a5cb816694158cb48520a2689647f20" :answer-field/choices ["q-332622/field-1/bb71dd18b06237165fae60aec9d1c4d85a5cb816694158cb48520a2689647f20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332622" :question/id #uuid "b5abf4eb-a16d-59fe-ae4c-da3f3734dace" :question/math-academy-id "q-332622" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(4\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha +\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -\\alpha +4\\beta =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{8}{17},\\beta =\\frac{32}{17}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{8}{17}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\frac{32}{17}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332622/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6af40e66-155c-57b8-b427-95259a2c1034"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d" :answer/id #uuid "85ea854b-d8b7-51af-83b0-064a065a2ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bc517654-ce33-508c-bd29-da4121261bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "04f0462e-6e03-57c4-a62c-02f42e8deaef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332847/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d" :answer-field/choices ["q-332847/field-1/e6408dd67b1afc95abbb665bf42824581c9c10a695d65e88eed0f0101b01631d" "q-332847/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847/field-2/79d49c858b5edf1148886533a125b5456a31f60d21c5cf9cde2af3490363835f" :answer/id #uuid "73051c56-7ac8-5c6e-bec0-51d977b29b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "332c06c4-9abb-51ef-8589-0246fb1d71b3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332847/field-2/79d49c858b5edf1148886533a125b5456a31f60d21c5cf9cde2af3490363835f" :answer-field/choices ["q-332847/field-2/79d49c858b5edf1148886533a125b5456a31f60d21c5cf9cde2af3490363835f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332847" :question/id #uuid "4ea7cd46-1bf9-5e23-9308-5262d4ec08d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-332847" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+16y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{-4x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+16{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))+16(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(16\\alpha +16\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+(-16\\alpha +16\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}16\\alpha +16\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)) \\\\ -16\\alpha +16\\beta =9\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{9}{32},\\beta =\\frac{9}{32}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{9}{32}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\frac{9}{32}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+(-\\frac{9}{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+(\\frac{9}{32})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332847/field-1" "q-332847/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7a2bbc-4172-591e-98eb-f7586d3ae06b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836/field-1/25ee8cd617d28f44b58dc455c95aa0562022965710763a78d34df7db21494c7c" :answer/id #uuid "164ba21e-1d3d-5b6d-b668-cf9f28054098" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{26}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8c7062ab-815e-5271-afda-43f6c16d869f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd9d25c-e771-5807-828e-3fef054d3388" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332836/field-1/25ee8cd617d28f44b58dc455c95aa0562022965710763a78d34df7db21494c7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-332836/field-1/25ee8cd617d28f44b58dc455c95aa0562022965710763a78d34df7db21494c7c" "q-332836/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836/field-2/373639edc999c13cd524175a2548129397ca51d52f19d81c2e9039575284cbe0" :answer/id #uuid "1d27fe34-2810-51f0-b98f-3b67e08ddb0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b82b58df-876e-5e10-940d-c1c611e0970a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332836/field-2/373639edc999c13cd524175a2548129397ca51d52f19d81c2e9039575284cbe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-332836/field-2/373639edc999c13cd524175a2548129397ca51d52f19d81c2e9039575284cbe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332836" :question/id #uuid "476bd23f-79bf-50d4-8989-1188aefe9497" :question/math-academy-id "q-332836" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{2x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n4\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-8{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-8(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(12\\beta -8\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-12\\alpha -8\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}12\\beta -8\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -12\\alpha -8\\beta =10\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{15}{26},\\beta =-\\frac{5}{13}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{15}{26}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{5}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+(-\\frac{15}{26})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-\\frac{5}{13})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332836/field-1" "q-332836/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7a2bbc-4172-591e-98eb-f7586d3ae06b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332793/field-1/4a310207db2ad397b97cb2c652e9b9e86cb8394d2c34f54288f870c015ecb7a4" :answer/id #uuid "436e7b10-7b16-5c7f-bc62-4023f424bf9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228083 :answer-field/correct "q-332793/field-1/4a310207db2ad397b97cb2c652e9b9e86cb8394d2c34f54288f870c015ecb7a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-332793/field-1/4a310207db2ad397b97cb2c652e9b9e86cb8394d2c34f54288f870c015ecb7a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332793/field-2/f1a2ca89759013056cc62a6e50b571ad9b450678de8de88df85a764527014179" :answer/id #uuid "e9c1ef25-2730-55c2-9222-df1266a9f25a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228082 :answer-field/correct "q-332793/field-2/f1a2ca89759013056cc62a6e50b571ad9b450678de8de88df85a764527014179" :answer-field/choices ["q-332793/field-2/f1a2ca89759013056cc62a6e50b571ad9b450678de8de88df85a764527014179"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-332793"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-9y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{3x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n3\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-9{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n3(-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))-9(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(6\\beta -9\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-6\\alpha -9\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6\\beta -9\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ -6\\alpha -9\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{4}{13},\\beta =-\\frac{6}{13}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{4}{13}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{6}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+(-\\frac{4}{13})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-\\frac{6}{13})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332875/field-1/fb0093c8ea34ea932961f2f469cac49613522e4712afdc5677ecb73fb0a40c4d" :answer/id #uuid "2e30853a-1dab-532d-8e61-a49458bfc95b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332875/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53741043-aab3-54ef-85da-76b6fc1cde4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332875/field-1/fb0093c8ea34ea932961f2f469cac49613522e4712afdc5677ecb73fb0a40c4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-332875/field-1/fb0093c8ea34ea932961f2f469cac49613522e4712afdc5677ecb73fb0a40c4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332875/field-2/132e1cd241207e66c7dbbf06921d1d208c974484a868d6a140eef445f2bf60c2" :answer/id #uuid "47d98d42-8268-5816-bea2-0689f5a62ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332875/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e091bd4c-7b33-5b7d-9d30-e543e29224fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332875/field-2/132e1cd241207e66c7dbbf06921d1d208c974484a868d6a140eef445f2bf60c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-332875/field-2/132e1cd241207e66c7dbbf06921d1d208c974484a868d6a140eef445f2bf60c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332875" :question/id #uuid "10d0f5cf-3c42-59ed-8eee-a85dd6e32991" :question/math-academy-id "q-332875" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-10y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=A{e}^{2x}\\,+\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n5\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-10{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n5(-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))-10(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(20\\beta -10\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+(-20\\alpha -10\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}20\\beta -10\\alpha =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)) \\\\ -20\\alpha -10\\beta =-7\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{11}{50},\\beta =\\frac{13}{50}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{11}{50}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+\\frac{13}{50}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+(\\frac{11}{50})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+(\\frac{13}{50})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332875/field-1" "q-332875/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7a2bbc-4172-591e-98eb-f7586d3ae06b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332875"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332999/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b81f55a2-6da0-5d98-8622-da63be0c5f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186319099 :answer-field/choices ["q-332999/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332974/field-1/a2775864840e57ce2db8d7e714c420548db9c161e569fd60a01a3e26f6e2160c" :answer/id #uuid "df6b8fa9-f18f-5f95-8880-57c3e3d9151f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{-4x}+3\\cos(2x)-6\\sin(2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332974/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5d0ebf7c-0c30-5c6f-929f-27a2a79ddddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332974/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7480e52-6175-5fb1-a113-8410ee27569c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332974/field-1/a2775864840e57ce2db8d7e714c420548db9c161e569fd60a01a3e26f6e2160c" :answer-field/choices ["q-332974/field-1/a2775864840e57ce2db8d7e714c420548db9c161e569fd60a01a3e26f6e2160c" "q-332974/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332974" :question/id #uuid "14e79ab9-95dd-579a-aae2-e3c97924b12a" :question/math-academy-id "q-332974" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=-30\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=-30\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $-30\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}=-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))+4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))=-30\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(2\\beta +4\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+(-2\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=-30\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\beta +4\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ -2\\alpha +4\\beta =-30\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =3,\\beta =-6.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-4\\cdot 0}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) & =1 \\\\ A+3-0 & =1 \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{-4x}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332974/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05d3144f-53da-5608-a07b-d1d5d672bf0b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
